<title>NETHERLANDS: Stork expects further growth in 1997.</title>
<headline>Stork expects further growth in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NAARDEN, Netherlands 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch industrial systems and services group Stork NV said on Tuesday it was positive about the company's prospects in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We assume further profit growth lies clearly ahead of us,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Earlier, Stork posted 1996 net profits of 137 million guilders, up from 1995's 108.3 million. Analysts had expected profits to rise to between 122 and 135 million guilders in 1996.  </p>
<p>Stork said its order book had increased by 922 million guilders in 1996 to 3,952 million guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
